<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- What the launcher needs to know about the word tile before it has ever drawn one.

     It arrives two cells square and resizes freely in both directions, down to a single
     row and up to the whole grid: the tile is one grid sized to its own box (WordWidget),
     so every shape between those two holds as many words as it fits, and none of them is
     a face this file has to name. A single row is worth allowing because the grid folds
     its cell to fit one — a strip of words across the top of a screen is a tile somebody
     wants. No maxResize pair: a launcher turns those dp into a SPAN against its WIDEST
     cell, so a ceiling meant to say "as wide as the screen" hands a phone four of its
     five columns and the three-across grid never appears; left out, the cap is the grid.

     updatePeriodMillis is thirty minutes because that is the shortest the platform will
     schedule — anything smaller is silently clamped. It is a CEILING on staleness rather
     than the refresh that matters: the app nudges the tile on every persist, so a phone
     in use redraws far more often, and this only covers the phone nobody has opened.

     The picker's thumbnail is the app's own mark. A placed tile only ever shows the
     learner's own box (docs/surfaces.md), and the picker cannot read one. -->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:minWidth="110dp"
    android:minHeight="110dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="2"
    android:targetCellHeight="2"
    android:minResizeWidth="110dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="50dp"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    android:previewImage="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/glance_default_loading_layout"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="1800000" />
